# Production build. SAME-ORIGIN API: the SPA (www.magizhmatrimony.com) calls a
# relative /api/v1 path, which CloudFront (distribution E39BG4XMB7DKLB) routes
# to the backend via a dedicated /api/* cache behavior. This makes the auth
# cookies (access_token/refresh_token) first-party, so the browser reliably
# sends refresh_token on /auth/refresh-token. Previously this pointed at the
# absolute https://api.magizhmatrimony.com/api/v1, which the browser treated as
# a third-party (cross-subdomain) request and dropped the refresh_token cookie
# -> the /auth/refresh-token endpoint always 401'd on reload.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api/v1

# The chat WebSocket handshake still goes DIRECTLY to the backend origin
# (SockJS/STOMP over CloudFront's static SPA origin isn't viable), so it must
# stay an absolute host — it is NOT routed through the /api/* behavior above.
VITE_WS_BASE_URL=https://api.magizhmatrimony.com

# Replace with the real reCAPTCHA site key registered for the production domain.
VITE_RECAPTCHA_SITE_KEY=6LeIxAcTAAAAAJcZVRqyHh71UMIEGNQ_MXjiZKhI
